Package: docdesigner
Title: Publication-Inspired Templates for Research PDFs and Slides
Version: 0.10.0
Authors@R: person("Joseph N.", "Cohen", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "joseph.cohen@qc.cuny.edu")
Description: Pandoc/R Markdown templates for research papers, book chapters,
    reports and briefs. Provides publication-inspired, token-driven
    style sets so researchers can produce polished, audience-aware PDF output
    from R and reproduce the look of well-known publications.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://jncohen.github.io/docdesigner/, https://github.com/jncohen/docdesigner
BugReports: https://github.com/jncohen/docdesigner/issues
Imports:
    rmarkdown,
    yaml
Suggests:
    knitr,
    pkgdown,
    xml2
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: pandoc (>= 3.1.8), XeLaTeX
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/Needs/website: pkgdown
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
